      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-02T00:43:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can this iteration throw ConcurrentModificationException? If so, I think that will be hard to debug because ConcurrentModificationException is not Parcelable and cannot be sent back to the caller of dump(). Would suggest catching the ConcurrentModificationException and re-throwing a parcelable exception such as IllegalStateException. You can find the list of parcelable exceptions here:\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/frameworks/base/core/java/android/os/Parcel.java;l\u003d341",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 766,
